When you do call {{{ retrieveCodeContextFunctionName }}}, note that `file_path`
may be either the file where the symbol is defined OR any file that
references/uses it: when the symbol isn't defined in `file_path`, the tool
automatically resolves the real definition via LSP go-to-definition, including
definitions that live in another repo file or in a third-party library/stdlib.
`reference_line` is only an optional disambiguator. Omit it normally: without
it, all occurrences are resolved and the resulting definitions are
de-duplicated. Set it only when you need to choose among reference/usage
occurrences that could resolve to different definitions. Its value must identify
the intended usage, not a declaration such as `func Something`.

